<title>BRAZIL: Brazil petrol production sets record.</title>
<headline>Brazil petrol production sets record.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petroleum production by Brazilian state-owned oil firm Petrobras set a record of 901,000 barrels per day, the company said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Average production in September stood at 815,138 bpd, a previous record.</p>
<p>Petrobras said 69.6 percent of the new record production, or 627,100 bpd, came from the Campos Basin.</p>
<p>-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
